ltitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(2,1,2)$, $B(3,4,2)$, $C(5,4,2).$" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524276 1072 #uuid "18deea5a-b54f-52df-a2ec-2c79bc3b4021" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524276 1074 "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+2k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j \\\\  & =⟨1,3,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(5i+4j+2k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+3j \\\\  & =⟨3,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0)i-(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-6k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\ 6 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524277 1080 "\\frac{6}{5}" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524277 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524277 1083 #uuid "229676e2-dcee-59b9-ac83-b20a4270b240" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524278 1080 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{13}" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524278 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524278 1083 #uuid "2ec8d433-d4ad-5c6a-af58-d6d95e54203b" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524279 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{113}}{13}" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524279 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524279 1083 #uuid "37b273cc-e0cb-5b4a-bf8e-08e164ef574f" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524271 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524280 1071 "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-1,-1,0)$, $B(-3,2,0)$, $C(-2,2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524280 1072 #uuid "3c269e70-e4c2-5782-b1f2-15eb40534125" 13194139535655 17592186045443 true] [17592186524280 1074 "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)-(-i-j) \\\\  & =-2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+2j)-(-i-j) \\\\  & =-i+3j \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & 